  "results": [
    {
      "id": "md2025_2282",
      "subset": "S5",
      "task_type": "cross-company-year-hybrid",
      "question": "In their Item 7 MD&A, which company explicitly states that they provide quantitative information about the impact of changes in volume and pricing on sales, and at which organizational level do they report this? Provide textual evidence from both ECL's FY2022 and LIN's FY2024 filings, and identify which financial table or note is referenced for additional segment detail.",
      "expected_answer": "ECL's FY2022 Item 7 states: 'We provide quantitative information about the material sales drivers including the impact of changes in volume and pricing and the effect of acquisitions and changes in foreign currency at the corporate and reportable segment level.' LIN's FY2024 Item 7 does not contain a similar explicit statement; instead it directs readers to 'Note 18 to the consolidated financial statements for additional information related to Linde’s reportable segments.' This Note 18 constitutes the financial table referenced for segment details.",
      "predicted_answer": "ECL (FY2022) explicitly states in its Item 7 MD&A that it provides quantitative information about the impact of changes in volume and pricing on sales, reporting this at both the **corporate and reportable segment level**. The text reads: \"We provide quantitative information about the material sales drivers including the impact of changes in volume and pricing and the effect of acquisitions and changes in foreign currency at the corporate and reportable segment level.\" [E1]\n\nLIN (FY2024) does **not** contain an equivalent explicit statement in its Item 7 MD&A about providing quantitative volume and pricing information. Instead, LIN presents volume/price/mix data in segment-level tables without a declaratory policy statement. Its segment tables show factors like \"Volume,\" \"Price/Mix,\" \"Cost pass-through,\" and \"Currency\" for each reportable segment (Americas, EMEA, APAC, Engineering, Other) [E2][E5][E8].\n\nFor additional segment detail, **LIN FY2024** refers readers to **Note 18** to the consolidated financial statements for information related to reportable segments [E4]. The evidence ledger for **ECL FY2022** does not contain a specific note reference for segment detail within the retrieved Item 7 excerpts; the MD&A refers generally to \"the consolidated financial statements and related notes included in this Form 10-K\" [E1].\n\nSources:\n[E1] ECL_2022.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations.\n[E2] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT'S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS\n[E4] LIN_2024.html — Item 1. BUSINESS\n[E5] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT'S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS\n[E8] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT'S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS",
